// Title: New DNS ServerLevelPluginDll Installed Via Dnscmd.EXE
// Sigma ID: f63b56ee-3f79-4b8a-97fb-5c48007e8573
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2017-05-08 | Modified: 2023-02-05
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, defense-impairment, T1574.001, T1112
// Description: Detects the installation of a DNS plugin DLL via ServerLevelPluginDll parameter in registry,
//   which can be used to execute code in context of the DNS server (restart required)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://medium.com/@esnesenon/feature-not-bug-dnsadmin-to-dc-compromise-in-one-line-a0f779b8dc83
//   - https://blog.3or.de/hunting-dns-server-level-plugin-dll-injection.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dnscmd_install_new_server_level_plugin_dll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\dnscmd.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/config" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/serverlevelplugindll")
